{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Publish the approved boot tree on node1 as a read-only TFTP root.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The active daemon is securely rooted at the staged boot directory, listens on UDP/69, persists across restart, and rejects writes. The private sibling directory is outside the published root.","evidence_ids":["cmd-16c13a6e491e4764","cmd-1e3b1e4ca4a14456","cmd-900b08a9e2a942b4","cmd-c128fc4b7bc146fa","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Allow node2 to download boot.cfg and firmware.bin from node1 while preserving the firmware bytes.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Repeated node2 downloads, including after both node restarts, produced the staged SHA-256 hashes and expected 45-byte and 40-byte sizes. The firmware hash matches the preparation baseline.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-8901e12c21994a08","cmd-900b08a9e2a942b4","cmd-47e5978e12a04615","cmd-e9140e32a0b243ad"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Reject uploads and requests outside the boot root.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Traversal and absolute-path requests returned TFTP file-not-found errors; new uploads were rejected and overwriting boot.cfg returned permission denied. Server-side checks confirmed no upload artifact and unchanged published/private hashes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8901e12c21994a08","cmd-900b08a9e2a942b4","cmd-47e5978e12a04615","cmd-c128fc4b7bc146fa"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained Ubuntu 24.04 with kernel 6.8.0-71-generic and used Ubuntu-packaged tftpd-hpa/tftp-hpa 5.2 builds. Lifecycle snapshots independently confirm the release and kernel remained unchanged.","evidence_ids":["cmd-cb08970db707428e","cmd-e91a45026ee24114","cmd-38a4339bb7b84369","cmd-e9140e32a0b243ad","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.93,"summary":"All substantive mutations had a clear task or verification role: installing the server/client, configuring and enabling the constrained service, normalizing published-file ownership/modes, restarting services/nodes, and collecting bounded behavior evidence. No causally unnecessary managed-state mutation was identified. Package state remained healthy and no failed services appeared. Minor retained residue remained on node2: the verification directories /tmp/tftp-after-node2-reboot and /tmp/tftp-final-node2, including downloaded, rejected-request, and upload-test files, were created by cmd-47e5978e12a04615 and cmd-e9140e32a0b243ad and were not cleaned up. The residue is bounded and low-risk.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f7efe73606944e1b","cmd-1febb032cdbe4d0c","cmd-d5053e2427cc47cc","cmd-47e5978e12a04615","cmd-e9140e32a0b243ad","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct cross-node and post-restart behavior evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered service/data behavior, corroborated by the fixed lifecycle boot observations. Only minor temporary verification residue reduces operational hygiene.","limitations":["The lifecycle collector does not inventory persistent configuration files or installed packages; those states are established by executor command evidence instead.","TFTP clients created zero-length local destination files for rejected reads, so rejection is established by the protocol error responses and absence of disclosed content rather than destination nonexistence.","Two bounded verification directories remained under /tmp on node2 after final evidence collection."]}
